+### Securely save an Apple Account login
+
+After a successful sign-in, choose whether to save the login. A separate local
+unlock passphrase (at least 12 characters, different from the Apple password)
+protects it. iSH has no OS keychain: scrypt derives an encryption key and
+XChaCha20-Poly1305 authenticates the saved email, password, developer session,
+signing private key and anisette cache. The unlock passphrase is never saved.
+Files are private (`0600`), with private storage directories (`0700`). Existing
+plaintext signing data is migrated when encrypted saving is enabled.
+
+Next time, unlock the saved login, unlock and update its password, use another
+account once, or forget the login and local signing data. Forgetting does not
+revoke Apple's certificate. A wrong local passphrase does not contact Apple.
+One-off accounts use an encrypted temporary cache removed when the run ends.
+
+### Select a pairing file from Minis / iSH
+
+The pairing step offers a directory browser and a full-path field, or use
+`siboot --pairing-file /root/phone.plist`. XML/binary RPPairing plists and JSON
+exports with matching public/private keys are supported. Classic lockdown
+pairing files cannot be used for this tunnel.
+
+The selected file is normalized into a private staging file and verified with
+the iPhone. Only after verification does it replace `rp_pairing_file.plist`
+**beside the actual siboot executable**. The source is preserved; a failed
+import leaves the previous pairing file untouched. Saved pairing files in the
+old `~/.siboot` location are migrated when no adjacent file exists.
+
+### Complete signing
+
+Signing discovers nested executable bundles at every depth, signs Mach-O
+images by their file headers (including deep dylibs and extensionless helpers),
+then seals ordinary `.config` files, hidden files and the remaining resources.
+A final resource audit rejects missing or changed seals before installation.
+Relative symlinks are sealed and preserved during AFC upload; links outside
+the app are rejected. The upload is checked before installation starts.
+
+### Retry a failed step
+
+When a step fails, the page keeps the completed steps and offers **Retry step**
+or **Stop**. Retry repeats that step, then continues. The downloaded IPA and
+Apple session stay available; an install retry reuses the signed app and opens
+a fresh tunnel. A handover retry only sends the pairing file again, without
+reinstalling. Cancelled prompts and sign-ins stop without offering a retry.
+In the terminal the same choice is **Retry this step?**.
+
+### Install a local IPA
+
+The page first offers **Download SideInstaller**, or a file picker for an
+`.ipa` already in Files. Pick it and tap **Use selected IPA**. The file is copied
+into Minis in small chunks and checked before the run continues. A failed
+import leaves the picker open to try again. Local files skip the GitHub check
+and release download; signing still needs Apple's servers, an Apple Account
+and LocalDevVPN. The uploaded copy is removed when the run ends.
+
+In the terminal, choose **Install a local IPA** and enter its path inside
+Minis, or pass it directly (quote paths containing spaces):
+
+```sh
+siboot --ipa "/path/to/My App.ipa"
+```
+
+The original file is left alone. Any app can be signed and installed this
+way; only SideInstaller receives SideInstaller's pairing-file handover and
+the **Open SideInstaller** button.
+
+These changes require a newly built siboot binary. The `bin/siboot-aarch64`
+already in this checkout and the upstream install command still run the
+published build; see [Building](#building) to rebuild and update its checksum.
+
